{"text": "# Sparrowhawk Youth Music Project — 2025 gift acknowledgments (working notes)\n\n*Prepared by Imogen Ferguson, development manager, for the bookkeeper. EIN 56-2740118. Letters must go out by Jan 31. Do not share outside finance: this has donor names next to amounts, and Schedule B is not public.*\n\n## Letters that need special wording\n\n**1. Eleanor Suzuki** (Mrs. Suzuki, 91 this year, our oldest donor; large print, please)\n- Gift of stock: 150 shares transferred 12/18/2025 from her account at Wexford Hale Securities, acct 8QR-204417, DTC confirmation WH25-1218-0093.\n- Value on the date of gift: $21,946.50 (mean of high and low). **The letter describes the shares, not the value.** She needs Form 8283 because it is over $5,000? No, publicly traded, Section A only.\n- Mail to 14 Kimberly Knoll Rd, Asheville, NC 28804. Her daughter Faith Okonedo opens the mail now (Eleanor has macular degeneration); copy faith.okonedo@postbox.example.\n\n**2. Vikram and Nandini Rao**\n- Monthly gift of $275 on Vikram's Amex ending 2586, twelve charges, $3,300.00 total. One charge (Aug 3) was refunded and re-run, so QuickBooks shows thirteen. It is twelve.\n- Gala table, $2,000, less goods and services of $640 (eight dinners at $80). Deductible: $1,360. This is a quid pro quo letter under IRC § 170(f)(8).\n- They asked to be listed as \"The Rao Family\". Address 305 Sunset Summit, Asheville 28804-1120. vik.rao@mailhaven.example, 828-555-0166.\n\n**3. Lyle Kaminski**\n- $7,500 by Visa, card number on the pledge form 4660 7563 0004 2082 (shred the form after entry; do NOT type the number into the CRM, last four only).\n- Given \"in memory of my husband Doug\" (Douglas Kaminski, our former board treasurer, d. April 2025). Use that wording exactly. Lyle does not want the gift listed in the annual report.\n- 828.555.0143; 22B Chestnut Mews, Asheville, NC 28801.\n\n## Gifts through someone else (no tax letter from us, thank-you only)\n\n| Source | Amount | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Beacon Charitable Gift Fund (donor-advised) | $10,000.00 | Grant BCG-2025-118845, advised by the Raos. Beacon is the donor of record. Check #0061877. |\n| Congregation Ohr Chadash sisterhood | $1,200 | Collected at their Hanukkah concert. Mrs. Suzuki's daughter-in-law organised it; several of our parents are members there. Cheque #4418. |\n| Pipefitters Local 512 | $750 | Instrument fund. Arranged by Patrick Leclerc, a member of the local and dad of one of our cellists. Money order 19-447720613. |\n\n## In-kind\n\n- Leclerc Honda of Asheville (Patrick's brother's dealership) lent a van for the tour. No value stated in the letter. Their EIN, if the auditor asks: 56-1193027.\n\n## Loose ends\n\n- Publication 1771 says $250 and up needs a written acknowledgment. Everything above qualifies except nothing; the Local 512 gift is from an organisation, still send one.\n- Mr. Rao wants a single year-end statement instead of twelve receipts. Fine.\n- Form 990 Schedule B: Suzuki, Beacon and Kaminski are over the threshold. — IF, 1/9/26", "kind": "Markdown document", "detail": "488 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Imogen Ferguson", "Eleanor Suzuki", "Vikram Rao", "Nandini Rao", "Lyle Kaminski", "Faith Okonedo", "Douglas Kaminski", "Raos", "Suzuki", "Patrick Leclerc", "Mr. Rao", "Kaminski"], "companies": ["Wexford Hale Securities", "Amex", "QuickBooks", "mailhaven", "example", "postbox", "IRC", "Beacon Charitable Gift Fund", "Congregation Ohr Chadash", "Pipefitters Local 512", "Leclerc Honda of Asheville"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Asheville", "Kimberly Knoll Rd", "Sunset Summit", "Chestnut Mews", "Beacon"], "health": [], "sensitive": ["macular degeneration", "d", "donor-advised", "Hanukkah"], "names": ["Imogen", "Eleanor Suzuki", "Vikram", "Nandini", "Lyle", "Douglas", "Patrick", "Mrs."]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs"